{{!--
Rows by tag, under « Les plus lus ». The sequence of forms is fixed by the theme so that two
neighbouring rows never share a form (Final-rangees-catalogue):
  1. shelf of 16:9 tiles   (row 1)          4. numbered text list, by date   (row 3)
  2. tag tiles « Rubriques » (most used tags) 5. collection banner             (row 4)
  3. 2:3 posters           (row 2)          6. one large post + four          (row 5)
Which tag fills each row: the theme setting « Home row N » (home_row_1 ... home_row_5, a tag slug,
Ghost Admin > Settings > Design > Homepage) when it is set; otherwise the Nth most used public tag.
A setting naming no existing public tag (e.g. "none") removes its row; a tag without posts has no row.
A tag pinned by one row never fills another: when the Nth most used tag is pinned in a setting (any row),
the row that would fall back on it is left out, so no tag appears twice (and every id row-<slug> is unique).
--}}

{{!-- 1. Shelf (16:9) --}}
{{#if @custom.home_row_1}}
  {{#get "tags" filter="slug:{{@custom.home_row_1}}+visibility:public" include="count.posts" limit="1"}}{{#foreach tags}}{{> "home/row-shelf"}}{{/foreach}}{{/get}}
{{else}}
  {{#get "tags" filter="visibility:public" include="count.posts" order="count.posts desc" limit="5"}}{{#foreach tags from="1" to="1"}}{{#match (concat "," @custom.home_row_1 "," @custom.home_row_2 "," @custom.home_row_3 "," @custom.home_row_4 "," @custom.home_row_5 ",") "~" (concat "," slug ",")}}{{else}}{{> "home/row-shelf"}}{{/match}}{{/foreach}}{{/get}}
{{/if}}

{{!-- 2. Tag tiles: the six most used public tags --}}
{{> "home/row-tags"}}

{{!-- 3. Posters (2:3) --}}
{{#if @custom.home_row_2}}
